[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "For Acyclovir, the dose varies by indication: acute treatment of herpes zoster is 800 mg orally every 4 hours (5 times daily) for 7 to 10 days; initial genital herpes is 200 mg every 4 hours (5 times daily) for 10 days; suppressive therapy is 400 mg twice daily; chickenpox in children is 20 mg/kg 4 times daily; no overall maximum daily dose is stated. For Acyclovir suspension, the dosing instructions are identical to oral acyclovir, with doses varying by indication (e.g., 800 mg orally 5 times daily for herpes zoster, 200 mg 5 times daily for genital herpes, 400 mg twice daily for suppressive therapy, and 20 mg/kg 4 times daily for chickenpox in children); no overall maximum daily dose is stated.",
